{
  "id": "typescript-15-type-level-programming-limits",
  "slug": "type-level-programming-limits",
  "title": "When to stop: readability versus clever types",
  "moduleId": "typescript-15-advanced-type-patterns",
  "order": 4,
  "hook": "Type-level programming has **readability** and **compile-time** costs — senior engineers know when to stop: Zod infer over 40-line conditionals, type budget per directory.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "What is this?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Deep conditionals/recursive mapped types slow tsc and block review. **Type complexity budget**: app=interfaces+zod; shared lib=utilities with review. **extendedDiagnostics** profiles slow files. **satisfies** pragmatic middle."
        },
        {
          "type": "glossary",
          "title": "Key terms",
          "entries": [
            {
              "term": "type budget",
              "longForm": "team convention",
              "plainDefinition": "Cap on type gymnastics per area.",
              "example": "no conditionals in features/"
            },
            {
              "term": "extendedDiagnostics",
              "longForm": "tsc perf",
              "plainDefinition": "Check time per file.",
              "example": "tsc --extendedDiagnostics"
            },
            {
              "term": "infer hell",
              "longForm": "nested infer",
              "plainDefinition": "Unreadable infer chains.",
              "example": "maintainer-only types"
            },
            {
              "term": "satisfies",
              "longForm": "pragmatic check",
              "plainDefinition": "Validate without widening.",
              "example": "cfg satisfies Config"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Why does it matter?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "One clever types.ts slows IDE for all. On-call cannot read 3-screen errors. Interview: know advanced AND when to refuse."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "tip",
          "title": "Interview trap: clever in prod",
          "body": "Want mechanism knowledge AND judgment to use Zod/codegen instead."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How it works step by step",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "title": "Mental model",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "runtime first",
              "body": "zod infer"
            },
            {
              "title": "named aliases",
              "body": "split complex types"
            },
            {
              "title": "measure compile",
              "body": "extendedDiagnostics"
            },
            {
              "title": "review radar",
              "body": "reject infer hell"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
